The symbolic theorem will use two reachability claims: an exact whole-function entry claim and one loop circularity over an arbitrary `ValSeq`. Its summary is structurally recursive over the semantics’ own `.ValSeq`/`vCons` constructors and includes both `Int` and `Bool`, matching the supplied `isinstance` rules. The only semantic lemma I’m introducing is the exhaustive equivalence `isIntV(V) = isInt(V) or isBool(V)`; it restates the fixed builtin’s existing cases and does not skip any program step.
